-- title:
--   Completion at a maximal ideal: complete local, with universal property
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative Noetherian ring and let $\mathfrak p \subseteq B$ be a maximal ideal. The assertion is that the $\mathfrak p$-adic completion $\hat B :=$ `AdicCompletion 𝔭 B` carries a local ring structure, is Noetherian, and is adically complete with respect to its maximal ideal, and that, for these structures, the following four statements hold: (i) the maximal ideal of $\hat B$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak p$ under the structure map $B \to \hat B$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_{\hat B} = \mathfrak p\,\hat B$ in the sense of `Ideal.map`; (ii) the composite of $B \to \hat B$ with the residue map $\hat B \to \hat B/\mathfrak m_{\hat B}$ is surjective; (iii) the kernel of that composite is exactly $\mathfrak p$, so that the residue field of $\hat B$ is canonically $B/\mathfrak p$; and (iv) for every commutative local Artinian ring $T$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : B \to T$ carrying each element of $\mathfrak p$ into the maximal ideal of $T$, there is a unique ring homomorphism $\Phi : \hat B \to T$ which is local (i.e. pulls back non-units to non-units) and satisfies $\Phi \circ (B \to \hat B) = \varphi$.
--
--   This packages the standard structure theory of the completion of a Noetherian ring at a maximal ideal — complete, local, Noetherian, with residue field $B/\mathfrak p$ — together with the universal property that continuous-by-nilpotence maps to Artinian local rings factor uniquely through the completion. It is the basic tool for producing coefficient rings and for identifying deformation rings with completions, and is used throughout the construction of the coefficient rings and of étale or flat base changes of such completions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AdicCompletion_exists_isLocalRing_and_existsUnique_lift_of_isArtinianRing.lean

